  "visualBrief": "Individual Polotsk Saint Sophia Cathedral: off-white lime-plaster Baroque twin-tower front with two actual open arched tiers per tower, narrower faceted attics/green caps and crosses; shaped central gable, tall arched glazing, recessed wood portal, pilasters and selected scroll/urn details. Broad green nave roof, rounded rear apse with small lantern, paired rounded side chapels/green domes/lanterns and low mapped envelope ranges. Four existing shared plaster/limestone/standing-seam metal/wood graphs, linear tints, metric UVs, flat normals and four browser levels. Fine stucco figures/iron scrollwork, inscriptions, full interiors, exact hidden rear details/roof joins and surveyed plaza thresholds are approximate or excluded.",
